IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-75, TARGETED: the Supervision of Financial Services (Provident Funds) Law, 5765-2005 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two items, I1 and then I2, each a reference as typed values, and tests them.
--   I1: item 13A of Part B of the First Schedule, as inserted by section 23 of the instrument printed in Sefer HaChukim (SH) 2507, cites section 24A(B)(8) and section 24B(A)(11); section 24A, as inserted by section 11 of the same instrument, prints a subsection (He) that gives the section an end date.
--   I2: the definition of the determining date, printed in SH 2932, cites section 34Vav(Dalet); section 34Vav, printed in the same issue, prints the subsections Alef, Bet and Gimel.
-- SEAT: a reader of the Law's printed text. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument, a place in the Law, a text of the Law as an instrument printed it, a provision of an instrument itself, a pointer inside a text, an end date printed in the Law, a commencement as the page prints it, a citation of a subsection, a section as printed, an item, and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in pf75-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read (the later instruments are listed in NOTES.md).
-- Hebrew letters that name a section or a subsection are written with Latin names in identifiers: Alef (the first letter), Bet, Gimel, Dalet, He, Vav, Zayin.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A date typed as an issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date.
-- A commencement is typed separately, and only where a page prints one.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A way a fact was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `official page image, with the later instruments listed in NOTES.md`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

DECLARE `A Hebrew letter` IS ONE OF
    Alef
    Bet
    Gimel
    Dalet
    He
    Vav
    Zayin

DECLARE `A kind of issue` IS ONE OF
    `Sefer HaChukim`
    `Kovetz HaTakanot`

-- An issue of Sefer HaChukim or of Kovetz HaTakanot. The issue date is the one the footer prints.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its kind` IS A `A kind of issue`
    `its issue number` IS A NUMBER
    `its issue date` IS A DATE

DECLARE `A division of the Law` IS ONE OF
    Section
    `Part B of the First Schedule`

-- A place in the Law: a section (number, optional letter) or an item of Part B of the First Schedule (number, optional letter), optionally a subsection, optionally a paragraph of it.
DECLARE `A place in the Law` HAS
    `its division` IS A `A division of the Law`
    `its number` IS A NUMBER
    `its letter` IS A MAYBE `A Hebrew letter`
    `its subsection` IS A MAYBE `A Hebrew letter`
    `its paragraph` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- A text of the Law as an instrument printed it. `its words` are copied from the ext: line above the value.
DECLARE `A printed text` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the place it is printed at` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A provision of an instrument itself (a section of an amending law or of an order), not a provision of the Law.
DECLARE `A provision of an instrument` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `its number as printed` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection` IS A MAYBE `A Hebrew letter`
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A pointer inside a text: the words as printed, and the place they name.
DECLARE `A pointer` HAS
    `the printed text that holds it` IS A `A printed text`
    `its words as printed` IS A STRING
    `the place it names` IS A `A place in the Law`

-- A subsection of the Law that gives its section an end date, with the date it prints and the Hebrew form of that date as printed.
DECLARE `An end date printed in the Law` HAS
    `the printed text that holds it` IS A `A printed text`
    `the words that give the end` IS A STRING
    `the section it ends` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the date it prints` IS A DATE
    `its Hebrew form as printed` IS A STRING

-- A commencement as the page prints it: the provision that prints it, the places it names (none where it names the instrument as a whole), the date and the Hebrew form of the date as printed.
DECLARE `A commencement as printed` HAS
    `the provision that prints it` IS A `A provision of an instrument`
    `the places it names` IS A LIST OF `A place in the Law`
    `the date it prints` IS A DATE
    `its Hebrew form as printed` IS A STRING

-- A citation of a subsection of a section, in words printed in an instrument.
DECLARE `A citation of a subsection` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the words that hold it` IS A STRING
    `its words as printed` IS A STRING
    `the section it names` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the subsection letter it names` IS A `A Hebrew letter`

-- A section as an instrument printed it: the subsection letters it prints, as read from the page images, and the section printed after it on the last page it is on.
DECLARE `A section as printed` HAS
    `the place` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed pages it is on` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the subsection letters it prints` IS A LIST OF `A Hebrew letter`
    `the section printed after it on its last page` IS A `A place in the Law`

-- A date printed in an instrument, with the words it is printed beside.
DECLARE `A printed date` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the date it prints` IS A DATE
    `its Hebrew form as printed` IS A STRING

-- An item of the row, with its two limbs.
DECLARE `An item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

GIVEN t IS A `A printed text`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed text contains the words` MEANS CONTAINS (t's `its words`) w

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first instrument was issued after the second` MEANS a's `its issue date` > b's `its issue date`

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two instruments are the same issue` MEANS
    (a's `its kind` EQUALS b's `its kind`) AND (a's `its issue number` EQUALS b's `its issue number`)

-- Two places are in the same section: the same division, number and letter, whatever the subsection or paragraph.
GIVEN a IS A `A place in the Law`, b IS A `A place in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two places are in the same section` MEANS
    (a's `its division` EQUALS b's `its division`)
    AND (a's `its number` EQUALS b's `its number`)
    AND (a's `its letter` EQUALS b's `its letter`)

-- I1: the end date is found in the words that print it: the words that give the end and the Hebrew form of the date are both in the printed text.
GIVEN e IS AN `An end date printed in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the end date is found in the words that print it` MEANS
    (CONTAINS (e's `the printed text that holds it`'s `its words`) (e's `the words that give the end`))
    AND (CONTAINS (e's `the printed text that holds it`'s `its words`) (e's `its Hebrew form as printed`))

-- I1: some subsection in the list gives the section an end date.
GIVEN s IS A `A place in the Law`, es IS A LIST OF `An end date printed in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section prints a subsection that ends it on a stated date` MEANS
    any (GIVEN e YIELD `the two places are in the same section` (e's `the section it ends`) s) es

-- I1, the question asked of the first pointer: the section the pointer names prints no subsection in the list that ends it on a stated date.
GIVEN p IS A `A pointer`, es IS A LIST OF `An end date printed in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section the pointer names prints no subsection that ends it on a stated date` MEANS
    NOT (`the section prints a subsection that ends it on a stated date` (p's `the place it names`) es)

-- I1: the places a commencement names, and the date it prints for one of them.
GIVEN c IS A `A commencement as printed`, pl IS A `A place in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the commencement names the place` MEANS elem pl (c's `the places it names`)

-- I2: does the section as printed print the letter the citation names?
GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a subsection`, s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section prints the letter the citation names` MEANS
    elem (c's `the subsection letter it names`) (s's `the subsection letters it prints`)

-- I2: every citation in the list that names the section names a letter the section prints.
GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`, cs IS A LIST OF `A citation of a subsection`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every citation of the section names a letter the section prints` MEANS
    all (GIVEN c YIELD (NOT (`the two places are in the same section` (c's `the section it names`) (s's `the place`))) OR (`the section prints the letter the citation names` c s)) cs

GIVEN d IS A `A printed date`, e IS A `A printed date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first date is earlier than the second` MEANS d's `the date it prints` < e's `the date it prints`

GIVEN c IS AN `An item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`
